# Wave H.g — Make admin IgnorePlugin gates real

## Problem

`apps/web/next.config.ts` claimed to strip Denali/Urban from the **client** bundle unless `ALLOW_*_WEB_PLUGIN=true`. Hostile audit correctly called this “hides, does not remove.” On trunk the gate was worse than advertised:

| Defect | Effect |
| ------ | ------ |
| Regex used `@app-cloud/…` | Package scope never matched `@app-tour/…` — **IgnorePlugin was a no-op** |
| Anchored to package **root only** (`…denali$`) | Real client imports are almost all **subpaths** (`…/host/…`, `…/plugin`, `…/settings/…`) and bypassed even a correct root regex |

So `ALLOW_DENALI_WEB_PLUGIN` / `ALLOW_URBAN_WEB_PLUGIN` did not control the client graph.

## Decision (H.g — harden the gate, do not remove it)

1. Fix package scope to `@app-tour`.
2. Match root **and** subpaths:

```text
/^@app-tour\/workspace-denali(\/|$)/
/^@app-tour\/workspace-urban(\/|$)/
```

3. Centralize the env→regex pairs in `apps/web/src/bootstrap/admin-client-workspace-ignore.mjs` so specs can assert the contract without parsing Next config prose. (**Superseded by Wave H.j** — see [`wave-h-manifest-ignore-plugin.mdoc`](./wave-h-manifest-ignore-plugin.mdoc); artifact is now `admin-client-workspace-ignore.generated.mjs`.)
4. Keep applying IgnorePlugin **only on the client** (`!isServer`) — server/codegen loaders still resolve packages for SSR/RSC.
5. Document operational law: product admin client features require `ALLOW_DENALI_WEB_PLUGIN=true` and/or `ALLOW_URBAN_WEB_PLUGIN=true` (smoke scripts + `infra/env/server.web.env.example` already set Denali; add Urban to env examples).

## Out of scope

- Removing IgnorePlugin entirely / `optionalDependencies` install-graph isolation (still breaks monorepo dynamic `import()` — Wave G)
- Manifest-driven IgnorePlugin list for every workspace id — **done in** [`wave-h-manifest-ignore-plugin.mdoc`](./wave-h-manifest-ignore-plugin.mdoc) (Wave H.j)
- Changing portal/marketing transpile strategy

## Rationale

True install isolation is a later wave. Until then the env gate must at least **mean what it says**. Fixing the dead `@app-cloud` typo + subpath coverage is the honest thin-shell step; deleting the gate without an install strategy would falsely claim isolation.

## Verify

```bash
rg '@app-cloud/workspace-(denali|urban)' apps/web/next.config.ts   # must be empty
node --test apps/web/test/wave-h-ignore-plugin-gate.spec.ts
```
